course: dictionary
lesson: 13766
title: Interruptions and breaks
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: An interruption is when something stops what is happening for a short time. Often a person stops someone from talking or working. «Sorry for the interruption, but the bell has rung.» The speaker stops for a moment, then carries on.
explain: Use the words around the word to find its meaning. «The film played without interruption for two hours.» Without interruption means there was no stopping at all. Try your meaning in the sentence: a break in the film does not fit, so the meaning is a stop or break, and it fits.
explain: In class, an interruption is when you talk while someone else is speaking. We wait our turn instead. «The power interruption turned off the lights for ten minutes.» Here the interruption is not a person. It is a break in the electricity.
fact: An interruption is when someone or something stops a person talking or an activity for a short time.
fact: An interruption can also be a break in something that should keep going, like electricity or a TV show.
fact: «Without interruption» means without any stopping or breaks.
fact: «Sorry for the interruption» is a polite way to say sorry for breaking in.
fact: Interruption is a noun, so it names a thing: an interruption, or interruptions.
exercise: «The film played without interruption for two hours.» What does without interruption mean? | Very loudly | With lots of breaks | Only for a short time | *Without any stopping or breaks
exercise: In class, what is an interruption? | Writing a story | Waiting quietly for your turn to speak | *Talking while someone else is speaking | Reading in the library
exercise: «The power interruption turned off the lights for ten minutes.» What was interrupted? | The children's lunch | The teacher's voice | The bell | *The electricity supply
test: What is a polite way to say sorry for breaking in? | Go away now | *Sorry for the interruption | Hello there | Excuse the noise
test: If a TV show has an interruption, what happens? | The volume gets quieter | *The show stops for a short time | The show never stops | A new episode starts
exam: «The class listened without interruption while Maya read her poem.» What does without interruption mean? | Very loudly | *Without anyone stopping or talking over her | Only for a short time | With lots of breaks
